Repair the following Java 6 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.
Print your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:
<repaired_code>
<your_repaired_code>
</repaired_code>
<confidence>
<your_confidence_score>
</confidence>
Do not provide any other text or markdown fences.

Here is the problem description:
<problem_description>
Little Petya loves training spiders. Petya has a board n × m in size. Each cell of the board initially has a spider sitting on it. After one second Petya chooses a certain action for each spider, and all of them humbly perform its commands. There are 5 possible commands: to stay idle or to move from current cell to some of the four side-neighboring cells (that is, one command for each of the four possible directions). Petya gives the commands so that no spider leaves the field. It is allowed for spiders to pass through each other when they crawl towards each other in opposite directions. All spiders crawl simultaneously and several spiders may end up in one cell. Petya wants to know the maximum possible number of spider-free cells after one second.
</problem_description>

Here is the Java 6 code you have to repair:
<original_code>
import java.io.*;
import java.util.*;

public class ProblemE {
    public static int w, h;
    public static final int INF = 9999999;
    public static Set<Integer> result = new HashSet<Integer>();

    public static void dfs(int col, int row, int mask) {
        if (col >= w) {
            result.add(mask);
            return;
        }
        if (row >= 1) {
            dfs(col+1, row, mask|(1<<col));
        }
        if (row <= h - 2) {
            dfs(col+1, row, mask|(1<<(col+w*2)));
        }
        if (col >= 1) {
            dfs(col+1, row, mask|(1<<((col-1)+w)));
        }
        if (col <= w - 2) {
            dfs(col+1, row, mask|(1<<((col+1)+w)));
        }
        dfs(col+1, row, mask|(1<<(col+w)));
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));
        String[] line = br.readLine().split(" ");
        w = Integer.parseInt(line[0]);
        h = Integer.parseInt(line[1]);
        if (w > h) {
            int tmp = w;
            w = h;
            h = tmp;
        }

        int[][] dp = new int[h+1][1<<(w*3)];
        for (int i = 0 ; i <= h ; i++) {
            Arrays.fill(dp[i], INF);
        }
        dp[0][0] = 0;

        for (int i = 0 ; i < h ; i++) {
            result.clear();
            dfs(0, i, 0);
            for (int j = 0 ; j < 1<<(w*2) ; j++) {
                if (dp[i][j] != INF) {
                    for (int res : result) {
                        int next = (res | j);
                        int nextn = next >> w;
                        int add = Integer.bitCount(next & ((1<<w) - 1));
                        dp[i+1][nextn] = Math.min(dp[i+1][nextn], dp[i][j] + add);
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        int answer = INF;
        for (int j = 0 ; j < 1<<(w*2) ; j++) {
            answer = Math.min(answer, dp[h][j] + Integer.bitCount(j));
        }
        System.out.println(h * w - answer);
    }
}
</original_code>
